## Environment configs

### `envs/backend-dev.hcl`

```hcl
bucket         = "acme-tfstate"
key            = "app-infra/dev/terraform.tfstate"
region         = "eu-central-1"
dynamodb_table = "acme-tfstate-lock"
encrypt        = true
kms_key_id     = "alias/acme-tfstate"
```

### `envs/backend-prod.hcl`

```hcl
bucket         = "acme-tfstate"
key            = "app-infra/prod/terraform.tfstate"
region         = "eu-central-1"
dynamodb_table = "acme-tfstate-lock"
encrypt        = true
kms_key_id     = "alias/acme-tfstate"
```

Separate `key` values give fully independent state files — a `prod` apply cannot touch `dev` state, and each can be planned/applied in isolation. (Workspaces would share one backend and one credential scope; distinct state keys plus distinct AWS accounts/roles is the stronger isolation and is what this layout uses.)

